WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:02.332
- People wanna understand Russia.

00:00:02.332 --> 00:00:04.941
So it's probably
time we brought that up.

00:00:04.941 --> 00:00:06.573
So the Internet Research Agency,

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.216
a Kremlin-linked social
media manipulation entity,

00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:11.309
actually began its
disinformation campaigns

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:12.392
in late 2014.

00:00:13.365 --> 00:00:15.500
It used all social
networks to grow audiences,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.728
every single one of them.

00:00:16.728 --> 00:00:18.260
Something just came out today that,

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.487
you know it's sort of like
this NSFW kind of thing,

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.270
but apparently they made
like some porn also,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.702
like they were everywhere, everywhere.

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:28.472
And as deep fakes become more prevalent

00:00:28.472 --> 00:00:29.781
I think we can continue to,

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:31.743
deep fakes are manipulated videos,

00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:35.634
so as the content that
is manipulatable changes,

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.498
the adversary grabs on to
the most bleeding-edge thing,

00:00:38.498 --> 00:00:42.076
recognizing that that's
where the least defense is,

00:00:42.076 --> 00:00:44.813
that those fronts are
really not well defended

00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:46.671
and not well monitored.

00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:50.567
So Russia really went hard on Facebook,

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.154
and so these are some of the, I think,

00:00:53.154 --> 00:00:55.966
God, there are dozens of
pages, I think, I'm sorry,

00:00:55.966 --> 00:00:58.139
I'm a little brain-dead
on my facts right now,

00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:01.257
47 or 67, but they had
a lot of these pages,

00:01:01.257 --> 00:01:02.958
this is just a handful of them.

00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:05.065
They, you can kind of,
you can probably gauge

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.512
what they are based on the names,

00:01:06.512 --> 00:01:09.626
and so what I wanna call
attention to here is Blacktivist,

00:01:09.626 --> 00:01:11.747
so this was a Black Lives Matter page,

00:01:11.747 --> 00:01:14.788
but it was just a little
bit more extreme, right?

00:01:14.788 --> 00:01:18.626
Defend the 2nd, gun rights,
little bit more extreme.

00:01:18.626 --> 00:01:21.857
LGBT United was a pro-LGBT family page,

00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:24.596
the person writing it was a lesbian

00:01:24.596 --> 00:01:26.958
and it was very pro-gay families,

00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:29.398
but it was just a little bit provocative.

00:01:29.398 --> 00:01:30.464
And actually what they were doing

00:01:30.464 --> 00:01:31.621
was they were serving the content

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:34.529
to people who were likely
to be opposed to it.

00:01:34.529 --> 00:01:36.527
So the pages, you know,

00:01:36.527 --> 00:01:38.129
they have relatively
normal-sounding names,

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:40.217
if you've been on Facebook
I'm sure you've seen pages

00:01:40.217 --> 00:01:42.050
with names very similar,

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:45.001
I'm sure you've seen content
that looks exactly like this,

00:01:45.001 --> 00:01:46.623
widely shared.

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:49.505
So here are two of the
memes, Army of Jesus

00:01:49.505 --> 00:01:51.663
and Secured Borders, you'll notice,

00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:52.940
they gave me this handy thing,

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:53.923
I don't know if it's actually on but,

00:01:53.923 --> 00:01:54.756
yeah, there ya go.

00:01:54.756 --> 00:01:57.182
So you'll notice that they
actually brand their content,

00:01:57.182 --> 00:01:58.817
and that's because they're
trying to look like

00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:02.807
you know, a community page
or a citizen journalist page,

00:02:02.807 --> 00:02:04.344
or an activist page.

00:02:04.344 --> 00:02:06.450
So all of the content
that these pages produced

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.226
had these marks which it
actually made it quite convenient

00:02:09.226 --> 00:02:11.121
for tracking them across the internet.

00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:12.067
But there's a couple of things

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.299
that I wanna just call attention to here,

00:02:14.299 --> 00:02:15.757
this is memetic propaganda,

00:02:15.757 --> 00:02:18.699
and we'll go into memes in a minute,

00:02:18.699 --> 00:02:20.727
but one thing that's
really interesting to note

00:02:20.727 --> 00:02:23.696
is the call to action, "Like
if you want Jesus to win."

00:02:23.696 --> 00:02:25.152
So when you like the content

00:02:25.152 --> 00:02:27.221
you're communicating back
to the social platform

00:02:27.221 --> 00:02:28.280
something about yourself,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.755
which makes it easier for them
to reach you in the future.

00:02:30.755 --> 00:02:32.600
You've just given a signal
that you are receptive

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.962
to this kind of content.

00:02:33.962 --> 00:02:36.089
If I'm running ads and
I have an ads budget,

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.183
I'm gonna wanna spend as
little money as possible,

00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:39.953
so I'm gonna wanna serve ads to people

00:02:39.953 --> 00:02:41.444
who've already engaged with my content,

00:02:41.444 --> 00:02:43.673
or done something to indicate to me

00:02:43.673 --> 00:02:45.525
that they like what I have to serve.

00:02:45.525 --> 00:02:47.512
And that's because that's
how I find my true believers,

00:02:47.512 --> 00:02:49.538
and as I said a propagandist
needs an audience,

00:02:49.538 --> 00:02:51.177
so that's how I'm gonna
continue to proselytize

00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:53.010
to the most receptive.

00:02:53.992 --> 00:02:56.344
Similarly if you like "If
you want Jesus to win,"

00:02:56.344 --> 00:02:58.264
Facebook will transmit that like

00:02:58.264 --> 00:03:01.004
to some percentage of the
people in your broader network,

00:03:01.004 --> 00:03:03.582
who it thinks will also
be receptive to this,

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.817
and so that's how we find
ourselves in a position

00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:08.657
where what you do and what you share

00:03:08.657 --> 00:03:10.401
directly impacts your friends,

00:03:10.401 --> 00:03:12.716
and how information spreads virally

00:03:12.716 --> 00:03:15.278
through small, vulnerable communities.

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:18.559
IRL, they ran events, they
literally had event pages.

00:03:18.559 --> 00:03:20.903
There was one notable instance in Texas

00:03:20.903 --> 00:03:22.665
where there was a pro-Muslim page

00:03:22.665 --> 00:03:25.268
and a pro-Texas secessionist page.

00:03:25.268 --> 00:03:27.128
They set up events, rallies,

00:03:27.128 --> 00:03:28.697
on the same day in the same place,

00:03:28.697 --> 00:03:30.992
trying to get the people
into the same place

00:03:30.992 --> 00:03:33.641
at the same time, and
they got a riot out of it.

00:03:33.641 --> 00:03:36.269
And these are people who
are sitting in Russia,

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:37.829
not even in the US,

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:40.169
getting two groups of
Americans to literally show up

00:03:40.169 --> 00:03:42.829
and have a fight in the streets in Texas.

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:46.822
So disinformation, in
order to be effective,

00:03:46.822 --> 00:03:48.978
must be 90% accurate,

00:03:48.978 --> 00:03:51.731
and this is where the studies
of human psychology come in

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.578
with propaganda,

00:03:52.578 --> 00:03:54.588
the fact that the content
that they're producing

00:03:54.588 --> 00:03:56.752
looked plausibly American.

00:03:56.752 --> 00:03:59.061
When I showed you those memes,
the first thing you think

00:03:59.061 --> 00:04:01.417
isn't Russian troll in
Siberia, maybe now it is,

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:03.270
but two years ago it
most definitely wasn't.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.688
And so that's where we think
they're producing content

00:04:06.688 --> 00:04:09.977
that is just, you know
it is so true looking,

00:04:09.977 --> 00:04:12.341
it's just like a little bit
out there to the fringe,

00:04:12.341 --> 00:04:13.672
and as we started digging into the pages,

00:04:13.672 --> 00:04:15.156
we did realize that there were moments,

00:04:15.156 --> 00:04:17.253
we were like, this is not
how a native English speaker

00:04:17.253 --> 00:04:18.379
would say this thing.

00:04:18.379 --> 00:04:21.875
There would be these
really funny long prose,

00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:23.829
like the way you learn
to write in third grade.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:26.381
Hilary Clinton is a terrible person,

00:04:26.381 --> 00:04:27.399
therefore it is important

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:28.816
that we do not elect her president,

00:04:28.816 --> 00:04:30.482
ergo,

00:04:30.482 --> 00:04:31.988
we must all vote for Donald Trump, right?

00:04:31.988 --> 00:04:33.119
And so the sort of extra,

00:04:33.119 --> 00:04:36.679
nobody running a Texas
secessionist page talks like that.

00:04:36.679 --> 00:04:37.826
(laughing)

00:04:37.826 --> 00:04:39.601
Not to stereotype, but let's be honest.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.670
(laughing)

